                    <p class=MsoNormal><span style="font-family:仿宋;mso-bidi-font-family:'Times New Roman';font-size:12.0000pt;
mso-font-kerning:1.0000pt;"><font face="仿宋"><p>"Instrumental Analysis" is a core foundational course for undergraduate pharmacy programs. It serves as a crucial bridge for translating "chemical principles into pharmaceutical applications." Focusing on the principles, operation of modern analytical instruments, and their applications in the pharmaceutical field, this course aims to develop students' ability to use instrumental analysis techniques to solve practical problems in pharmaceutical R&D, production, quality control, and clinical monitoring. It also lays a core skill foundation for students' future engagement in work such as pharmaceutical testing, pharmaceutical R&D, and clinical pharmacy.</p></font></span><span style="font-family:'Times New Roman';mso-fareast-font-family:仿宋;font-size:10.5000pt;
mso-font-kerning:1.0000pt;"><o:p></o:p></span></p>
